SWEET WLAN stage 3 run D (patch 0132, docs/research/43a-xnu-stage3-chip-writes.md row W14 and unknown X4), boot-arg sweetwlan=6 (= run C of 0131, then W14; levels 1-5 behave as in 0131).
W14: read backplane address 0 (BAR2 window 0, offset 0; all-ones or a failed read is a stop, the value is logged), store the first dword of the image (DHD resetinstr: dhd_pcie.c:3934-3936, 10198-10227), read it back; a word that does not hold it (X4: ROM bank alias) is a stop that stores nothing else (restore: none).
Pure part (bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_wr.h): new deny-by-default tuple SWT_RESET0 (run 4, once, needs W13, value = image word 0 of the pinned firmware, decided in the one swl_wr()). Before any store at level 6 the firmware identity is pinned: container FW entry length 1764018 and CRC32 0x1153ccff (review 0130 finding 8). The NVRAM entry is not pinned (CRC against its container record only). W14 re-checks the image and the pin (AP-74).
Glue (bsd/dev/sweet_wlan.c): sw3_wr() allows BAR2 window 0 offset 0 only at level 6 and only the container's first dword (sw_hw.l3, sw_hw.rv).
Final line: "SWEET WLAN: stage 3 level 6 done w14 old=<hex> new=<hex> vars=<n> token=<hex> crc=<hex>".
Tests: shim/wlan_wr_host_test.c, tools/test_wlan_wr_mutants.py. HW-WRITE path: not yet reviewed.

